1. display_board()

Purpose: To display the current game board.

FUNCTION display_board
    Print first row of board
    Print separator line
    Print second row of board
    Print separator line
    Print third row of board
END FUNCTION



2. get_move(player)

Purpose: To take the position from the current player.

FUNCTION get_move(player)
    Repeat
        Ask the player to enter a position from 1 to 9

        If the input is a number
            Return the number
        Otherwise
            Display "Please enter a number"
    Until a valid number is entered
END FUNCTION


3. validate_move(move)

Purpose: To check whether the player's move is valid.

FUNCTION validate_move(move)

    If move is less than 1 OR greater than 9
        Return False

    If the selected position is already occupied
        Return False

    Otherwise
        Return True

END FUNCTION


4. check_winner(player)

Purpose: To check whether a player has won.

FUNCTION check_winner(player)

    Check all 3 rows
    Check all 3 columns
    Check both diagonals

    If any row, column, or diagonal
    contains the same player's symbol
        Return True

    Otherwise
        Return False

END FUNCTION



5. check_draw()

Purpose: To check whether the game is a draw.

FUNCTION check_draw

    If all positions of the board are filled
        Return True

    Otherwise
        Return False

END FUNCTION
6. switch_player(player)

Purpose: To change the turn from one player to another.

FUNCTION switch_player(player)

    If current player is X
        Change player to O

    Otherwise
        Change player to X

    Return the new player

END FUNCTION


7. reset_game()

Purpose: To start a new game with an empty board.

FUNCTION reset_game

    Create a new empty board
    Make all 9 positions empty

END FUNCTION


8. play_game()

Purpose: To control the complete game.

FUNCTION play_game

    Repeat

        Reset the board

        Set starting player as X

        Repeat

            Display the board

            Get move from current player

            Check whether the move is valid

            If move is not valid
                Show error message
                Ask for move again

            Otherwise
                Place player's symbol on the board

                Check if the player has won

                If player has won
                    Display winner
                    Stop current game

                Check if the board is full

                If board is full
                    Display draw
                    Stop current game

                Change the player

        Until game is over

        Ask the user if they want to play again

    Until user chooses No

    Display thank-you message

END FUNCTION


Overall Pseudocode Flow
START
   ↓
Create empty 3×3 board
   ↓
Start Player X
   ↓
Display Board
   ↓
Get Player Move
   ↓
Validate Move
   ↓
Invalid? → Ask Again
   ↓
Place X or O
   ↓
Check Winner
   ↓
Winner? → Display Winner
   ↓
Check Draw
   ↓
Draw? → Display Draw
   ↓
Switch Player
   ↓
Repeat Game
   ↓
Play Again?
   ↓
YES → Reset Board
   ↓
NO → END
